# Build output
build/
.vs/
out/

# Third-party binaries and anything extracted from them.
#
# NO art belonging to another mod is tracked or shipped. The keycap SWFs in flash/ are
# SkyUI's and Untarnished UI's own; their terms allow modification, not redistribution, so
# they stay on your disk and out of this repository entirely -- including out of the FOMOD.
# The repository and its build artifacts carry exactly one SWF, dist/Interface/MMOHotbar/
# Hotbar.swf, which is our own build (tools/build_hud_swf.py) and embeds nothing of anyone
# else's. See flash/README.md for how to produce a keycap set for your own UI.
*.swf
!dist/Interface/MMOHotbar/Hotbar.swf
/Skyui/
/Untarnished/
flash/**/build/
flash/**/work/
/package/

# Reverse-engineering scratch: Hex-Rays output of SkyrimSE.exe is Bethesda's code.
/reverse/

# Vendored copy of DIII used as a reference while porting swfhelper.
# The parts actually used live in src/swfhelper/ with attribution.
/Dynamic-Inventory-Icon-Injector/

# Local tooling notes
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.clinerules/

# Local-only asset experiments (user-owned Photoshop/SWF exports, tooling
# scratch). Never part of the build or the FOMOD package.
# The name has a space, so it is anchored with a slash on both ends. Quoting it
# ("...") would NOT work: gitignore has no quoting, so the quote characters
# would become part of the pattern and it would match nothing.
/Asset dont push to git/
/dist/Hotbar.swf.xml
/tools/_out/
/tools/swfdump/
__pycache__/

# Reverse-engineering scratch: a throwaway CommonLibSSE-NG checkout plus the
# one-off analysis/export scripts used while porting the HUD movie.
/_tmp/
